;; (inherit-state <this> (method-of-type net-powerup NAME)) at link time for
;; whichever fields (:exit, :code, :event) neither override supplies. But
;; net-powerup.gc is a total stub (no forms landed at all, this worktree's own
;; goal_src), so that method-of-type read is null at link time and
;; scripts/check_state_inherit.py flags it. A fresh scoped decode of
;; net-powerup against this worktree's own types (netpowerup-decode scratch
;; proj, config-override {"allowed_objects": ["net-powerup"]}) does not clear
;; it: (top-level-login net-powerup) fails outright ("Decompiler type system
;; did not know the type of symbol *powerup-collide-results*. Add it!"), and
;; the method-set! calls that assign net-powerup's own idle/wait-respawn/
